WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:02.562
Oof.

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:05.820
Ouch!

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:08.150
In the climatic fight scene in "The Hunt,"

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:10.340
you see a lot of falling on the floor,

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:11.290
which should hurt,

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:12.960
but what you don't see is that

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.440
under a layer of vinyl made
to look like real flooring,

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.020
the floor is actually all foam,

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.500
according to the director.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.670
To make this elaborate fight scene work,

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:24.890
the filmmakers built an entire set

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:26.770
with each stunt in mind.

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:29.200
A set that was meant to be destroyed.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.100
This left the film's production designer

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.240
with the tough job of building sets

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.180
that were tailor-made to
fit the needs of a scene

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.110
without the audience ever noticing.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:41.403
Warning: spoilers ahead.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:45.247
In "The Hunt," a group
of conservative Americans

00:00:45.247 --> 00:00:48.510
is kidnapped by a group of
wealthy liberal Americans

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:50.220
and attacked for sport.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:52.470
No surprise, the satirical film

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.453
was met with much controversy.

00:00:55.310 --> 00:00:57.210
The film culminates as Crystal,

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.520
played by Betty Gilpin,

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.350
faces off against Athena,

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:01.740
played by Hilary Swank,

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:04.480
who helped organize the hunt
near her sprawling manor

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.210
where the fight takes place.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.740
When director Craig Zobel

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:09.580
was given the script for "The Hunt,"

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:11.560
all it indicated was that the climax

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.320
would be an epic head to head,

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.170
so he worked with the stunt coordinators,

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:17.830
special effects team,
and production designer

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:19.290
to choreograph a fight scene

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.410
that was a standout moment of the movie.

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:22.590
Craig Zobel: We wanted this whole fight

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:24.220
to just feel more messy and real,

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:25.940
and that drove a lot of the decisions

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:27.240
that we were making.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.920
The production designer and I, you know,

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.630
had all these kind of ideas
that were built around

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:35.010
building this jungle gym of a set.

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:36.530
Narrator: To map out the fight,

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.310
the stunt coordinators constructed

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:40.160
their own version of the home

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.180
out of cardboard boxes,

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:45.380
which stood in for the
60-foot-by-50-foot set.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:47.010
While working with the cardboard model,

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:49.010
the stunt team came up with the idea

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:51.860
of turning the kitchen
island into a stunt piece

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:53.980
by having the characters vault across it.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.950
While production designer Matthew Munn

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.170
had already planned to
have a kitchen island,

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.590
he now had to retrofit and redesign it

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:02.770
to ensure it was strong and sturdy enough

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:04.940
to support this one stunt.

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:06.720
To pull off the move successfully,

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:08.880
the island was built out of strong wood

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.970
and painted to look like concrete.

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:13.010
Then the top was removed and replaced

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:14.160
with a foam pad,

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.720
similar to how they used foam

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.550
underneath the vinyl floor covering.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:22.187
Zobel: Kind of like a
kid's playhouse foam floor

00:02:22.187 --> 00:02:23.620
for certain parts of it.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.160
Narrator: The two characters also fight

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:26.720
on top of the kitchen table.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:29.287
Like with the island, they
needed something sturdy,

00:02:29.287 --> 00:02:32.000
but they also wanted something
aesthetically pleasing,

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.980
so the production designer and decorator

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:35.772
picked out a rustic-looking table

00:02:35.772 --> 00:02:37.610
that fit in with the rest of the set.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:39.960
But because they knew it
would have to handle a lot,

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:42.140
they made sure the solid wood table

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:44.100
also had a steel base.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.460
Even average household items were chosen

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:47.880
and strategically placed

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.280
so they could be picked
up and used as weapons.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:52.920
Like this light fixture,
which both looks cool

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:54.660
and turned out to be practical.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:55.993
Athena: That was good.

00:02:57.459 --> 00:02:59.080
Narrator: And this food-processor blade,

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.480
which was Zobel's idea,

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.590
because it's something he has been

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:03.430
afraid of his whole life.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:05.520
Almost all the props you see,

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.160
from cabinets to jars,

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:08.600
are breakaway props,

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:11.210
which means they're built
to be safely broken.

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:12.560
Zobel: What I learned
is, once you're working

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:13.893
with this many breakaway items,

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:15.301
you do a lot of practice runs

00:03:15.301 --> 00:03:17.210
before you break them.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.937
Narrator: The next stunt was perhaps

00:03:18.937 --> 00:03:21.160
the most difficult one to shoot:

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:23.010
moving the fighters from the kitchen

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.150
to the living room.

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:26.110
To make this transition more dynamic,

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:28.080
the filmmakers decided they wanted to use

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.580
this unusual double-sided fireplace,

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:33.220
which the production design
team would need to build.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:35.610
Zobel saw a double-sided fireplace

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:38.060
while location scouting at a real house

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:40.500
and thought it would
be perfect for a stunt.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:42.510
The fireplace was built with your standard

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:44.070
drywall and concrete,

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:46.860
but they laid special
propane lines underground

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:48.570
that the special effects team could use

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:50.540
to increase the height of the flames

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:53.320
as the stunt double went
through the fireplace.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:56.110
The opening of the fireplace
was originally smaller,

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:58.020
but after some experimentation,

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:59.510
they expanded it so that it was

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:02.080
5 feet wide by 3 feet tall.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:03.650
It's a dangerous move,

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:05.170
so as an extra precaution,

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:06.980
they soaked the stunt double's clothes

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.320
with a fire retardant.

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:09.430
Then, under that,

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:12.880
she wore protective CarbonX and fire gel

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:14.970
to prevent her skin from burning.

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:18.587
Following this, Athena fires
at Crystal with her gun

00:04:18.587 --> 00:04:20.603
and hits the chimney. For that shot,

00:04:20.603 --> 00:04:23.600
Munn said the chimney was
altered to fit the move.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:24.890
They took a piece out of it,

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:26.730
replaced it with hard foam,

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:28.420
and then rigged it with squibs

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:30.680
for the perfect shotgun effect.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:33.470
Athena then chases Crystal up the stairs,

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:35.290
where they duke it out some more.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:36.810
But Crystal would eventually need

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:38.650
to get back downstairs somehow.

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:41.000
That's where these big
ropes came in handy.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.960
In the manor, they're meant
to be large art pieces,

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:46.840
but the team knew they could
double as a stunt piece.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:48.270
For the first part of the stunt,

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:51.050
Gilpin's stunt double was
connected to two lines

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:53.520
in a Y shape that were
attached to her harness.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.890
The lines went through
pulleys above the set,

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:57.070
which were then redirected

00:04:57.070 --> 00:04:59.230
to a pole station across the room.

00:04:59.230 --> 00:05:01.230
A stunt rigger made sure the stuntwoman

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:04.060
got just the right amount
of tension on her lines.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:06.760
Too much tension, and the
stunt would look fake.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:07.940
Not enough tension,

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:10.370
and she would peel off
the rope right away.

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:11.860
For the second part of the stunt,

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:14.400
she dangled about eight
feet off the ground.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:15.605
At the count of...

00:05:15.605 --> 00:05:17.249
Director: Three, two, one.

00:05:17.249 --> 00:05:18.800
Narrator: She would be pulled forward.

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.337
Then, once the rigger heard this sound,

00:05:21.337 --> 00:05:22.770
[crack]
he had to make sure

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:24.880
to drop her at just the right speed

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:27.260
so she fell directly onto this table.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.730
Knowing that she would land on it,

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:31.080
this had to be built as a breakaway table,

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:32.240
and the legs on the table

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:33.870
had to be constructed in such a way

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:37.010
that they would break immediately
on impact for this stunt.

00:05:37.010 --> 00:05:39.500
Meanwhile, because the
rope had to collapse,

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:42.520
it was held up with specially
made breakaway brackets,

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:43.700
which you can see here.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:46.020
According to Zobel, they
had enough materials

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.150
to do this fall four times.

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:49.841
In the end, he says he got it done

00:05:49.841 --> 00:05:51.760
in just one or two takes.

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:54.140
While the interior was
shot on a soundstage,

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:55.900
it still had to match the actual

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:58.270
exterior of the house shown on screen,

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:00.100
a real house in Louisiana.

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:02.310
So one element the production design team

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:04.020
had to match with the real house:

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:06.560
a hallway with big glass windows.

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:08.690
It served as the key part of the set

00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:10.840
to move the fight from inside the house

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:12.450
to this small courtyard.

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:15.270
The window turns into an
active part of the action

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:16.370
at the moment when Crystal

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:18.360
tries to throw Athena through it.

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:20.752
On the first try, the
window doesn't break,

00:06:20.752 --> 00:06:22.660
and then it does on the second try.

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:24.270
In reality, the windows were made

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:25.790
out of a tempered glass,

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:28.290
which they chose
specifically for this move.

00:06:28.290 --> 00:06:30.190
This type of glass is strong enough

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:32.898
to not break immediately,
but when it does,

00:06:32.898 --> 00:06:34.670
it breaks into tiny pieces

00:06:34.670 --> 00:06:36.640
as opposed to sharp shards.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:38.780
The stunt actresses
were attached to a rope,

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:40.700
which was attached to something stationary

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:42.170
known as a dead man,

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:44.130
allowing them to bang up against the glass

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:46.160
without being pulled through it.

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:47.780
Then, for the second attempt,

00:06:47.780 --> 00:06:49.590
Munn said the special effects team

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:51.330
rigged the glass with explosives

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:53.900
that were timed to go
off at the exact moment

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:56.450
the two characters needed
to go through the glass.

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:58.470
The glass was also retrofitted

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:00.140
to allow for this pulley system

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.630
put together by the stunt team,

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:03.350
which would then launch the characters

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:04.960
out into the courtyard.

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:06.340
Staging the scene this way

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:09.020
gave them an excuse to
move the fight outside

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:10.730
and then come back around the kitchen

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:12.080
for the fight's conclusion.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:14.360
Their transition from
one side of the house

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:16.040
to the other via the courtyard

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:17.700
was captured in one move

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:19.430
by this camera on a track.

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:21.170
Zobel, the cast, and crew

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:23.260
managed to film the entire sequence

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:25.810
over five long 12-hour days

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:27.520
at the very end of the shoot.

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:29.480
Building the set to support the fight

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:32.880
allowed them to shoot everything
safely and efficiently,

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:34.770
while still looking spontaneous

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:36.770
instead of overly choreographed.

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:38.330
While big parts of the set,

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:40.120
like windows and the fireplace,

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:41.420
were most crucial,

00:07:41.420 --> 00:07:44.960
even the most unexpected
objects and set decoration

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:46.410
helped advance the fight,

00:07:46.410 --> 00:07:48.770
like this expensive bottle of Champagne.

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:50.630
Zobel knew he wanted it there

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:53.740
for Crystal to grab at the
end of the fight as a reward,

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:55.130
but what he didn't know

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:57.910
was how perfect the moment
where Athena catches it

00:07:57.910 --> 00:07:59.230
would turn out to be.

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:02.370
Zobel: When we go to shoot
that portion of the scene,

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:03.480
on the very first take,

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:07.010
Hilary kind of dove and did
this amazing football catch

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:08.850
that I certainly did not anticipate,

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:11.060
and I don't think anybody
on set anticipated

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:13.150
her really going for it that much.

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:16.650
A cheer erupted on set

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:18.034
as she caught the Champagne.

00:08:18.034 --> 00:08:22.050
Hilary Swank: [laughing] Oh! Oh, my God.

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:23.648
The reaction after is funny.

00:08:23.648 --> 00:08:25.345
It's like I'm a masochist.

00:08:25.345 --> 00:08:26.537
[laughing]

00:08:26.537 --> 00:08:27.804
Come for more.

